# 17. Lifecycle Management

I created a Lifecycle Management policy.

The policy was:

```text
Blob type: Block Blob
Prefix: web-logs/
Condition: Older than 30 days
Action: Move to Cool
```

The policy was stored in:

```text
lifecycle-policy.json
```

Example:

```json
{
  "rules": [
    {
      "enabled": true,
      "name": "move-old-logs-to-cool",
      "type": "Lifecycle",
      "definition": {
        "filters": {
          "blobTypes": [
            "blockBlob"
          ],
          "prefixMatch": [
            "web-logs/"
          ]
        },
        "actions": {
          "baseBlob": {
            "tierToCool": {
              "daysAfterModificationGreaterThan": 30
            }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

I applied the policy using:

```bash
az storage account management-policy create \
  --resource-group $RG \
  --account-name $STORAGE \
  --policy @lifecycle-policy.json
```

The policy was successfully created.

### Lifecycle vs Manual Tier Change

The difference is:

```text
Manual
Blob
 ↓
Immediately change tier
 ↓
Cool
```

while Lifecycle Management is:

```text
Blob
 ↓
Condition is evaluated
 ↓
After 30+ days
 ↓
Automatically move to Cool
```

The Lifecycle policy does not necessarily execute immediately after creation.

