# Key Troubleshooting Lessons

When Azure Storage access does not work:

1. Check the Storage Account configuration.
2. Check whether public network access is disabled.
3. Check the Private Endpoint.
4. Check the Private Endpoint IP.
5. Check Private DNS.
6. Check DNS resolution from the VM.
7. Check TCP connectivity to port 443.
8. Check Managed Identity authentication.
9. Check RBAC permissions.
10. Check the Storage API response.
11. Distinguish management-plane problems from data-plane problems.
12. Do not change the network design just to install a tool unless it is actually necessary.

The most important troubleshooting lesson from this lab was:

> **Separate DNS, network, authentication, authorization, and application problems instead of treating every failure as a network problem.**

